        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/432915?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The documentation for <code class=\"notranslate\">fetch</code> includes a table in the \"Exceptions\" section with little examples for lots of the exceptions that can be thrown. We usually don't do this.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Also, most of the exceptions listed are some version of \"options properties were invalid according to the rules given in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RequestInit\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/RequestInit</a>\" - it's better surely to state these rules once, in that page, and then say here that the exception is thrown if these rules are broken.<br>\n(for one thing, we are inconsistent: for instance, we say that <code class=\"notranslate\">method</code> must be valid according to its definition, but not that <code class=\"notranslate\">credentials</code> must be valid).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Maaaybe we ought to keep these examples, or some of them, in the \"Examples\" section. I'm not sure they are that useful though.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/40802",
            "title": "Simplify fetch exceptions",
            "date_modified": "2025-08-20T00:18:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-08-19T23:40:06.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "wbamberg",
                "url": "https://github.com/wbamberg"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/143106292?u=b3c5814362982b570863d2bb4e99cc0cc32ec862&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Adds <code class=\"notranslate\">form</code> HTML attribute, providing all the supported elements with links for <code class=\"notranslate\">form</code> attribute.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">These changes ensure that <code class=\"notranslate\">form</code> attribute have its own standalone page and help the reader know about this attribute in a centralized place.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR might need <code class=\"notranslate\">label</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">meter</code>, and <code class=\"notranslate\">progress</code> BCD updates. Plus, these elements <code class=\"notranslate\">meter</code> , <code class=\"notranslate\">object</code> , <code class=\"notranslate\">output</code> might have limited support or no support at all after some research.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #28375.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1835534009\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28375\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/28375/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/28375\">#28375</a></p>\n",
